[description]

This package provides an in-memory store for [term geo/track] definitions, with memoized calculation
of extended attributes.

[para] The base data is pulled from a backing store, a [package map::track::store::fs] or any other
object providing the API described in section [term {Store API}] of [package map::track::store::fs]. The memory store adds derived attributes, like the length or the
center of a [term geo/track], and the pixel coordinates needed to draw the [term geo/track] on a map at
the various zoom levels. It is the store expected by [package map::track::map-display] and
[package map::track::table-display].

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]

[call [cmd ::map::track::store::memory] [arg storeName] [arg store]]

Creates a new store object named [arg storeName] on top of the backing store [arg store], and
returns the fully qualified name of its command. The [arg storeName] can be [const %AUTO%] to
generate a unique name.

[para] The [arg store] is the name of the command of the backing store, an object providing the
methods [method ids], [method get], and [method visible] as described in section
[term {Store API}] of [package map::track::store::fs]. It is not destroyed together with the memory
store.

[call [arg storeName] [method ids]]

Returns the list of the ids of all [term geo/track]s. This method is delegated to the backing
store.

[call [arg storeName] [method visible] [arg geobox]]

Returns the list of the ids of the [term geo/track]s visible in the geographical box [arg geobox].
This method is delegated to the backing store.

[call [arg storeName] [method get] [arg id]]

Returns the attributes of the [term geo/track] with the given [arg id], a dictionary. The attributes
are computed on the first request for an [arg id] and then cached. Throws an error if the [arg id]
is not known to the backing store.

[para] The dictionary contains
all the keys returned by the backing store, i.e. at least [const names] and [const geo] (see
[package map::track::file]), extended with the following derived attributes:

[list_begin definitions]
[def [const bbox]]
The geographical bounding box of the track, a list of minimal latitude, minimal longitude, maximal
latitude, and maximal longitude.

[def [const center]]
The center of the bounding box, a list of latitude and longitude.

[def [const diameter]]
The largest distance between any two vertices of the track, in meters.

[def [const length]]
The length of the track, from its first to its last vertex, in meters.

[def [const parts]]
The number of segments of the track, i.e. the number of vertices minus one.
[list_end]

[call [arg storeName] [method pixels] [arg id] [arg zoom]]

Returns the track with the given [arg id] in pixel coordinates of the map at the given [arg zoom]
level, as a list of points, each a list of x and y coordinates (see [package map::slippy]). The
track is simplified for display: vertices which are only a few pixels apart are merged, and
vertices which do not visibly change the shape are dropped. The result is cached for each
combination of [arg id] and [arg zoom].

[call [arg storeName] [method destroy]]

Destroys the store.

[list_end]

[para] All other methods are delegated to the backing store as well.

[para] The methods [method ids], [method get], [method visible], and [method pixels] are the API
used by [package map::track::map-display]. [package map::track::table-display] uses [method ids] and
[method get], and requires the derived attributes. Any object providing these methods with the
same results can be used in place of a [package map::track::store::memory].

[section EXAMPLE]

[example_begin]
package require map::track::store::fs
package require map::track::store::memory

map track store fs     TrackFiles /path/to/directory
map track store memory Tracks     TrackFiles

foreach id [lb]Tracks ids[rb] {
    set track [lb]Tracks get $id[rb]
    puts "[lb]lindex [lb]dict get $track names[rb] 0[rb]: [lb]format %.1f [lb]expr {[lb]dict get $track length[rb] / 1000.}[rb][rb] km"
    puts "  [lb]llength [lb]Tracks pixels $id 15[rb][rb] points to draw at zoom level 15"
}
[example_end]

